IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-interests`
IMPORT `sgb2-s164-register-of-shareholdings`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 164A -- the power to require disclosure of directors' emoluments -- and s 165 -- the general duty to make disclosure.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. s 164A: members holding 10% of the members, or 5% of the issued shares, can serve a notice requiring the emoluments of the directors to be disclosed; the company must then
-- prepare and audit a statement (14 days, or longer if the Registrar allows), send it to those entitled to notice of general meetings (14 days after the audit) and lay it before the next
-- general meeting. s 165: every director and chief executive officer must tell the company about his or her holdings (so that the company can keep the s 164 register), within 2 business days,
-- and the company must pass the notice to the other directors and chief executive officers within 7 days. Business days are counted by the keel's `period:` function with the public holidays supplied.

§ `Section 164A(1): the notice, and the three duties it triggers`

-- (1), the trigger: a notice "sent by or on behalf of" (a) at least 10% of the members (excluding the company itself if registered as a member) or (b) a member or members with at least 5% of the
-- issued shares (excluding treasury shares), "requiring the emoluments and other benefits received by the directors of the company or of a subsidiary to be disclosed".
-- The percentages are cross-multiplied, so no division is used.
-- src:14220 | 164A.—(1) If a company is served with a notice sent by or on
-- src:14221 | behalf of —
-- src:14223 | (a) at least 10% of the total number of members of the
-- src:14224 | company (excluding the company itself if it is registered as
-- src:14225 | a member); or
-- src:14227 | (b) a member or members with at least 5% of the total number
-- src:14228 | of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury
-- src:14229 | shares),
-- src:14231 | requiring the emoluments and other benefits received by the directors
-- src:14232 | of the company or of a subsidiary to be disclosed, the company
-- src:14233 | must —
@ref s 164A(1) (src:14220-14233)
GIVEN `the company has been served with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the emoluments and other benefits received by the directors of the company or of a subsidiary to be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members who sent the notice, or on whose behalf it was sent` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares, excluding treasury shares, held by the member or members who sent the notice or on whose behalf it was sent` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(1) the notice is one that the company must act on` MEANS
    IF    `the company has been served with the notice`
      AND `the notice requires the emoluments and other benefits received by the directors of the company or of a subsidiary to be disclosed`
      AND (   (`the number of members who sent the notice, or on whose behalf it was sent` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` TIMES 10)
           OR (`the number of issued shares, excluding treasury shares, held by the member or members who sent the notice or on whose behalf it was sent` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` TIMES 5))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company is served with a notice sent by or on behalf of (a) at least 10% ... or (b) ... at least 5% ..., requiring the emoluments ... to be disclosed, the company must" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 164A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 164A(1)(c) prepare the statement and cause it to be audited`
    `s 164A(1)(d) send a copy of the audited statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings`
    `s 164A(1)(e) lay the audited statement before the next general meeting`

-- (c): "within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may allow". The 14 days run from the day the company is served: the paragraph names no starting point, and the service of the notice is the only event
-- the subsection names (fork F-164A-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:14235 | (c) within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may
-- src:14236 | allow, prepare or cause to be prepared and cause to be
-- src:14237 | audited a statement showing the total amount of
-- src:14238 | emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by
-- src:14239 | each of the directors of the company and each director of a
-- src:14240 | subsidiary; including any amount paid by way of salary, for
-- src:14241 | the financial year immediately preceding the service of the
-- src:14242 | notice;
@ref s 164A(1)(c) (src:14235-14242)
GIVEN `the number of days the Registrar allows, where it is longer than 14 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 164A(1)(c) the number of days the company has to prepare the statement and cause it to be audited` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the Registrar allows, where it is longer than 14 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)` GREATER THAN 14
    THEN `the number of days the Registrar allows, where it is longer than 14 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)`
    ELSE 14

-- src:14235 | (c) within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may
-- src:14236 | allow, prepare or cause to be prepared and cause to be
-- src:14237 | audited a statement showing the total amount of
-- src:14238 | emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by
-- src:14239 | each of the directors of the company and each director of a
-- src:14240 | subsidiary; including any amount paid by way of salary, for
-- src:14241 | the financial year immediately preceding the service of the
-- src:14242 | notice;
@ref s 164A(1)(c) (src:14235-14242)
GIVEN `the day the company was served with the notice` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the company has to prepare the statement and cause it to be audited` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the statement had been prepared and audited` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(1)(c) the statement was prepared and audited in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company was served with the notice` `the day the statement had been prepared and audited` `the number of days the company has to prepare the statement and cause it to be audited` Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must (c) within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, prepare or cause to be prepared and cause to be audited a statement" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (c), the contents: the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each director of the company and each director of a subsidiary, including salary, for the financial year
-- immediately preceding the service of the notice. "Emoluments" is s 4(1)'s term, read by the caller.
-- src:14235 | (c) within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may
-- src:14236 | allow, prepare or cause to be prepared and cause to be
-- src:14237 | audited a statement showing the total amount of
-- src:14238 | emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by
-- src:14239 | each of the directors of the company and each director of a
-- src:14240 | subsidiary; including any amount paid by way of salary, for
-- src:14241 | the financial year immediately preceding the service of the
-- src:14242 | notice;
@ref s 164A(1)(c) (src:14235-14242)
GIVEN `the statement shows the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each of the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement shows the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each director of a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes any amount paid by way of salary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is for the financial year immediately preceding the service of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(1)(c) the statement is the statement the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the statement shows the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each of the directors of the company`
      AND `the statement shows the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each director of a subsidiary`
      AND `the statement includes any amount paid by way of salary`
      AND `the statement is for the financial year immediately preceding the service of the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement showing the total amount of emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by each of the directors of the company and each director of a subsidiary; including any amount paid by way of salary, for the financial year immediately preceding the service of the notice" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- src:14244 | (d) when the statement mentioned in paragraph (c) has been
-- src:14245 | audited, within 14 days send a copy of the statement to all
-- src:14246 | persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the
-- src:14247 | company; and
@ref s 164A(1)(d) (src:14244-14247)
GIVEN `the day the statement had been prepared and audited` IS A DATE
      `the day the company sent the copy` IS A DATE
      `the company sent a copy to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(1)(d) the company sent the copy of the audited statement in time to all the persons entitled` MEANS
    IF    `the company sent a copy to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the statement had been prepared and audited` `the day the company sent the copy` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the statement mentioned in paragraph (c) has been audited, within 14 days send a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14249 | (e) lay the statement before the next general meeting of the
-- src:14250 | company held after the statement is audited.
@ref s 164A(1)(e) (src:14249-14250)
GIVEN `the company laid the statement before the next general meeting of the company held after the statement was audited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(1)(e) the company laid the audited statement before the next general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company laid the statement before the next general meeting of the company held after the statement was audited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ... (e) lay the statement before the next general meeting of the company held after the statement is audited" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- The three duties as regulative rules. (e) has no period in days: it falls due when the next general meeting is held, so the days from the audit to that meeting are an input
-- (the date of the meeting is s 175's question, a later wave).
-- src:14235 | (c) within 14 days or such longer period as the Registrar may
-- src:14236 | allow, prepare or cause to be prepared and cause to be
-- src:14237 | audited a statement showing the total amount of
-- src:14238 | emoluments and other benefits paid to or received by
-- src:14239 | each of the directors of the company and each director of a
-- src:14240 | subsidiary; including any amount paid by way of salary, for
-- src:14241 | the financial year immediately preceding the service of the
-- src:14242 | notice;
@ref s 164A(1)(c) (src:14235-14242)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the company has to prepare the statement and cause it to be audited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164A act`
`s 164A(1)(c) the company must prepare the statement and cause it to be audited within the days allowed after it is served with the notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164A(1)(c) prepare the statement and cause it to be audited`
    WITHIN `the number of days the company has to prepare the statement and cause it to be audited`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not prepare the statement of directors' emoluments and cause it to be audited within 14 days, or the longer period the Registrar allowed, after it was served with the notice"

-- src:14244 | (d) when the statement mentioned in paragraph (c) has been
-- src:14245 | audited, within 14 days send a copy of the statement to all
-- src:14246 | persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the
-- src:14247 | company; and
@ref s 164A(1)(d) (src:14244-14247)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164A act`
`s 164A(1)(d) the company must send a copy of the audited statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings within 14 days after the audit` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164A(1)(d) send a copy of the audited statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the audited statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings within 14 days after the statement was audited"

-- src:14249 | (e) lay the statement before the next general meeting of the
-- src:14250 | company held after the statement is audited.
@ref s 164A(1)(e) (src:14249-14250)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the audit to the next general meeting of the company held after the statement is audited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164A act`
`s 164A(1)(e) the company must lay the audited statement before the next general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164A(1)(e) lay the audited statement before the next general meeting`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the audit to the next general meeting of the company held after the statement is audited`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the next general meeting of the company held after the statement was audited was held and the statement was not laid before it"

§ `Section 164A(2): the offence`

DECLARE `s 164A(2) penalty` HAS
    `s 164A(2) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 164A(2) the longest imprisonment, in years (0: the subsection provides none)` IS A NUMBER

-- src:14255 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:14256 | and every director of the company shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:14257 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 164A(2) (src:14255-14257)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 164A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164A(2) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `default is made in complying with section 164A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every director of the company shall be guilty of an offence" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); split site (i), fork F-164A-2 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is a director of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company and every director of the company" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i))

-- src:14255 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:14256 | and every director of the company shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:14257 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 164A(2) (src:14255-14257)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 164A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 164A(2) penalty`
`s 164A(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 164A` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is a director of the company`)
    THEN JUST (`s 164A(2) penalty` OF 10000, 0)   -- "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000"; the subsection names no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "the company and every director of the company" where "default is made in complying with this section"

§ `Section 165(1) and (10): the notice every director and chief executive officer must give`

DECLARE `s 165(1) kind of notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 165(1)(a) the particulars relating to shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options and contracts`
    `s 165(1)(b) the particulars of a change in those particulars`
    `s 165(1)(c) the events and matters affecting or relating to the person that the company needs for section 173A`
    `s 165(1) some other notice`

DECLARE `s 165 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 165(1)(a) give the company written notice of the particulars relating to shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options and contracts`
    `s 165(1)(b) give the company written notice of the particulars of the change`
    `s 165(1)(c) give the company written notice of the events and matters affecting or relating to the person`
    `s 165(3) send a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers`

-- (10): "Subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to a person (a) who is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company; and (b) who is required to make disclosure of the matters
-- referred to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) of this section under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001". "Listed" is s 4(1)'s term; the duty under the other Act is a fact.
-- src:14385 | (10) Subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to a person —
-- src:14387 | (a) who is a director or chief executive officer of a listed
-- src:14388 | company; and
-- src:14393 | (b) who is required to make disclosure of the matters referred
-- src:14394 | to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) of this section under
-- src:14395 | section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001.
@ref s 165(10) (src:14385-14395)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required to make disclosure of the matters referred to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) of section 165 under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(10) subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company` AND `the person is required to make disclosure of the matters referred to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) of section 165 under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says to whom "subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply" and says nothing of a person outside it, to whom subsection (1)(a) and (b) applies by its own terms

-- (1): the duty, by kind of notice. The person must be a director or chief executive officer of the company; (a) and (b) are limited to "such particulars ... as are necessary for the purposes of
-- compliance by the firstmentioned company with section 164 that are applicable in relation to him or her", and (c) to "such events and matters ... as are necessary for the purposes of compliance by the
-- company with section 173A that are applicable in relation to him or her".
-- src:14261 | 165.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of a company
-- src:14262 | must give written notice to the company —
-- src:14264 | (a) of such particulars relating to shares, debentures,
-- src:14265 | participatory interests, rights, options and contracts as
-- src:14266 | are necessary for the purposes of compliance by the
-- src:14267 | firstmentioned company with section 164 that are
-- src:14268 | applicable in relation to him or her;
-- src:14270 | (b) of particulars of any change in respect of the particulars
-- src:14271 | referred to in paragraph (a) of which notice has been given
-- src:14272 | to the company including the consideration (if any)
-- src:14273 | received as a result of the event giving rise to the
-- src:14274 | change; and
-- src:14276 | (c) of such events and matters affecting or relating to himself
-- src:14277 | or herself as are necessary for the purposes of compliance
-- src:14278 | by the company with section 173A that are applicable in
-- src:14279 | relation to him or her.
@ref s 165(1) (src:14261-14279)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 165(1) kind of notice`
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars, change, events or matters are necessary for the company's compliance with the section the paragraph names and are applicable in relation to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to the person by subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(1) the person must give the company written notice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is that of "Every director and chief executive officer of a company", with no "only"; the subsection says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 165(1) some other notice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists three kinds of notice, (a) to (c), without "only"
         WHEN `s 165(1)(c) the events and matters affecting or relating to the person that the company needs for section 173A`
              THEN (IF `the particulars, change, events or matters are necessary for the company's compliance with the section the paragraph names and are applicable in relation to the person`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such events and matters ... as are necessary for the purposes of compliance by the company with section 173A that are applicable in relation to him or her" limits the notice in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit
         OTHERWISE
              (IF `subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to the person by subsection (10)`
               THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1)(a) and (b) does not apply to a person (a) who is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company; and (b) who is required to make disclosure ... under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001" (a flat negative)
               ELSE IF `the particulars, change, events or matters are necessary for the company's compliance with the section the paragraph names and are applicable in relation to the person`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such particulars ... as are necessary for the purposes of compliance by the firstmentioned company with section 164 that are applicable in relation to him or her" limits the notice in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit

§ `Section 165(2): within 2 business days`

-- (2)(a): within 2 business days after (i) the date the director became a director or the chief executive officer became a chief executive officer, or (ii) the date the person became a registered holder of
-- or acquired an interest in the shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or contracts, "whichever last occurs". (The rendering prints this tail as a second "(a)".)
-- src:14285 | (a) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(a), within
-- src:14286 | 2 business days after —
-- src:14288 | (i) the date on which the director became a director or
-- src:14289 | the chief executive officer became a chief executive
-- src:14290 | officer, as the case may be; or
-- src:14292 | (ii) the date on which the director or chief executive
-- src:14293 | officer (as the case may be) became a registered
-- src:14294 | holder of or acquired an interest in the shares,
-- src:14295 | debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or
-- src:14296 | contracts,
-- src:14298 | (a) whichever last occurs; and
@ref s 165(2)(a) (src:14285-14298)
GIVEN `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, as the case may be` IS A DATE
      `the date the person became a registered holder of, or acquired an interest in, the shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or contracts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 165(2)(a) the date from which the 2 business days run` MEANS
    IF `the date the person became a registered holder of, or acquired an interest in, the shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or contracts` GREATER THAN `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, as the case may be`
    THEN `the date the person became a registered holder of, or acquired an interest in, the shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or contracts`
    ELSE `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, as the case may be`

-- The window is counted in business days by the keel's function, with the public holidays supplied (P8). The act is "not later than" the last day: a notice given on the day of the event itself is in time, which the
-- keel's window form (the day after the event onwards) would not allow (fork F-165-2 in NOTES.md).
