-- src:14290 | officer, as the case may be; or
-- src:14292 | (ii) the date on which the director or chief executive
-- src:14293 | officer (as the case may be) became a registered
-- src:14294 | holder of or acquired an interest in the shares,
-- src:14295 | debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or
-- src:14296 | contracts,
-- src:14298 | (a) whichever last occurs; and
@ref s 165(2)(a) (src:14285-14298)
GIVEN `the day the 2 business days run from` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(2)(a) the notice of the particulars was given within 2 business days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice was given` AT MOST `s 165(2) the last day for the notice` `the day the 2 business days run from` `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must be given (a) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(a), within 2 business days after" the later date (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14303 | (b) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(b), within
-- src:14304 | 2 business days after the occurrence of the event giving rise
-- src:14305 | to the change mentioned in that paragraph.
@ref s 165(2)(b) (src:14303-14305)
GIVEN `the day of the event giving rise to the change` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(2)(b) the notice of the change was given within 2 business days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice was given` AT MOST `s 165(2) the last day for the notice` `the day of the event giving rise to the change` `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must be given ... (b) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(b), within 2 business days after the occurrence of the event giving rise to the change" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The duties as regulative rules. (1)(a) and (1)(b) carry the 2 business days of (2); (1)(c) has no period in (2) (which names only (1)(a) and (1)(b)): see the rule after them.
-- src:14261 | 165.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of a company
-- src:14262 | must give written notice to the company —
-- src:14264 | (a) of such particulars relating to shares, debentures,
-- src:14265 | participatory interests, rights, options and contracts as
-- src:14266 | are necessary for the purposes of compliance by the
-- src:14267 | firstmentioned company with section 164 that are
-- src:14268 | applicable in relation to him or her;
-- src:14270 | (b) of particulars of any change in respect of the particulars
-- src:14271 | referred to in paragraph (a) of which notice has been given
-- src:14272 | to the company including the consideration (if any)
-- src:14273 | received as a result of the event giving rise to the
-- src:14274 | change; and
-- src:14276 | (c) of such events and matters affecting or relating to himself
-- src:14277 | or herself as are necessary for the purposes of compliance
-- src:14278 | by the company with section 173A that are applicable in
-- src:14279 | relation to him or her.
@ref s 165(1) (src:14261-14279)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company who is required to make the disclosure under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of calendar days from the day the 2 business days run from to the last day for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 165 act`
`s 165(1)(a) and (2)(a) the director or chief executive officer must give the company written notice of the particulars within 2 business days` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company who is required to make the disclosure under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
         MUST `s 165(1)(a) give the company written notice of the particulars relating to shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options and contracts`
         WITHIN `the number of calendar days from the day the 2 business days run from to the last day for the notice`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the director or chief executive officer did not give the company written notice of the particulars within 2 business days after the later of the day the person became a director or chief executive officer and the day the person became a registered holder of or acquired an interest in the shares, debentures, participatory interests, rights, options or contracts"

-- src:14270 | (b) of particulars of any change in respect of the particulars
-- src:14271 | referred to in paragraph (a) of which notice has been given
-- src:14272 | to the company including the consideration (if any)
-- src:14273 | received as a result of the event giving rise to the
-- src:14274 | change; and
@ref s 165(1) (src:14270-14274)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company who is required to make the disclosure under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of calendar days from the day of the event to the last day for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 165 act`
`s 165(1)(b) and (2)(b) the director or chief executive officer must give the company written notice of the change within 2 business days` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer of a listed company who is required to make the disclosure under section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
         MUST `s 165(1)(b) give the company written notice of the particulars of the change`
         WITHIN `the number of calendar days from the day of the event to the last day for the notice`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the director or chief executive officer did not give the company written notice of the change within 2 business days after the event giving rise to it"

-- (1)(c) has no period: s 165(2) names only (1)(a) and (1)(b). A "must" with no deadline can never reach BREACH, so the rule is listed under "Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md.
-- src:14276 | (c) of such events and matters affecting or relating to himself
-- src:14277 | or herself as are necessary for the purposes of compliance
-- src:14278 | by the company with section 173A that are applicable in
-- src:14279 | relation to him or her.
@ref s 165(1)(c) (src:14276-14279)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 165 act`
`s 165(1)(c) the director or chief executive officer must give the company written notice of the events and matters` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 165(1)(c) give the company written notice of the events and matters affecting or relating to the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 165(3): the company passes the notice on, within 7 days`

-- src:14309 | (3) A company must, within 7 days after it receives a notice given
-- src:14310 | under subsection (1), send a copy of the notice to each of the other
-- src:14311 | directors and chief executive officers of the company.
@ref s 165(3) (src:14309-14311)
GIVEN `the day the company received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the company sent the copy to each of the other directors and chief executive officers` IS A DATE
      `the company sent a copy to each of the other directors and chief executive officers of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(3) the company sent a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers in time` MEANS
    IF    `the company sent a copy to each of the other directors and chief executive officers of the company`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the notice` `the day the company sent the copy to each of the other directors and chief executive officers` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, within 7 days after it receives a notice given under subsection (1), send a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers of the company" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14309 | (3) A company must, within 7 days after it receives a notice given
-- src:14310 | under subsection (1), send a copy of the notice to each of the other
-- src:14311 | directors and chief executive officers of the company.
@ref s 165(3) (src:14309-14311)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 165 act`
`s 165(3) the company must send a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 165(3) send a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the notice to each of the other directors and chief executive officers within 7 days after it received the notice"

§ `Section 165(4) and (5): the defence of not being aware, and the presumption of awareness`

DECLARE `s 165(4) kind of failure` IS ONE OF
    `s 165(4) a failure to comply with subsection (1)(a)`
    `s 165(4) a failure to comply with subsection (1)(b)`
    `s 165(4) a failure to comply with subsection (2)`
    `s 165(4) another failure`

-- (4): "It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with subsection (1)(a) or (b) or with subsection (2) if the defendant proves that his or her failure was due to his or her not being aware of a fact or
-- occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence and that (a) he or she was not so aware on the date of the information or summons; or (b) he or she became so aware less than 7 days
-- before the date of the summons."
-- src:14317 | (4) It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with
-- src:14318 | subsection (1)(a) or (b) or with subsection (2) if the defendant proves
-- src:14319 | that his or her failure was due to his or her not being aware of a fact or
-- src:14320 | occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the
-- src:14321 | offence and that —
-- src:14323 | (a) he or she was not so aware on the date of the information or
-- src:14324 | summons; or
-- src:14326 | (b) he or she became so aware less than 7 days before the date
-- src:14327 | of the summons.
@ref s 165(4) (src:14317-14327)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 165(4) kind of failure`
      `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the defendant's not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant was aware of that fact or occurrence by the date of the information or summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days before the date of the summons on which the defendant became aware (ignored where the defendant was not aware by that date)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(4) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 165(4) another failure` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with subsection (1)(a) or (b) or with subsection (2)" limits the defence in its own wording, with no "only", and the case falls outside the limit
    OTHERWISE
        (IF    `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the defendant's not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence`
           AND (   (NOT `the defendant was aware of that fact or occurrence by the date of the information or summons`)
                OR `the number of days before the date of the summons on which the defendant became aware (ignored where the defendant was not aware by that date)` LESS THAN 7)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence ... if the defendant proves that his or her failure was due to his or her not being aware of a fact or occurrence ... and that (a) he or she was not so aware on the date of the information or summons; or (b) he or she became so aware less than 7 days before the date of the summons" (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences: when X is not proved, JUST FALSE for that provision's defence, worded 'this section gives no defence on these facts')

-- (5): a person "is conclusively presumed to have been aware at a particular time of a fact or occurrence (a) of which the person would, if the person had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of his or
-- her affairs, have been aware at that time; or (b) of which an employee or agent of the person, being an employee or agent having duties or acting in relation to his or her master's or principal's interest or
-- interests in a share in or a debenture of or participatory interest issued by the company concerned, was aware or would, if he or she had acted with reasonable diligence ..., have been aware at that time."
-- src:14329 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), a person is conclusively
-- src:14330 | presumed to have been aware at a particular time of a fact or
-- src:14331 | occurrence —
-- src:14333 | (a) of which the person would, if the person had acted with
-- src:14334 | reasonable diligence in the conduct of his or her affairs,
-- src:14335 | have been aware at that time; or
-- src:14337 | (b) of which an employee or agent of the person, being an
-- src:14338 | employee or agent having duties or acting in relation to his
-- src:14339 | or her master’s or principal’s interest or interests in a share
-- src:14340 | in or a debenture of or participatory interest issued by the
-- src:14341 | company concerned, was aware or would, if he or she had
-- src:14342 | acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of his or her
-- src:14343 | master’s or principal’s affairs, have been aware at that
-- src:14344 | time.
@ref s 165(5) (src:14329-14344)
GIVEN `the person would, had the person acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of his or her affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an employee or agent having duties or acting in relation to the person's interest or interests in a share in or a debenture of or participatory interest issued by the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that employee or agent was aware, or would, had he or she acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware, of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(5) the person is conclusively presumed to have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` MEANS
    IF    `the person would, had the person acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of his or her affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time`
       OR (`the person has an employee or agent having duties or acting in relation to the person's interest or interests in a share in or a debenture of or participatory interest issued by the company concerned` AND `that employee or agent was aware, or would, had he or she acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware, of the fact or occurrence at that time`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two cases of a conclusive presumption of awareness for the purposes of subsection (4) and does not say that a person in neither is presumed unaware

§ `Section 165(6) to (8): terms, interests, and matters already in the old register`

