`s 165(8) section 164 and this section do not require the matter to be entered in the register or notified to the company` MEANS
    IF `the matter is shown in the register kept by the company in accordance with the repealed section 134 as in force immediately before 5 October 1973`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in section 164 or this section requires a company to enter in its register or requires a director to give notice to the company of matters that are shown in the register kept ... in accordance with the repealed section 134" removes the duty for those matters and says nothing of any other

§ `Section 165(9): the offences`

DECLARE `s 165(9) penalty` HAS
    `s 165(9) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 165(9) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `s 165(9) the further fine for each day the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- src:14375 | (9) Any director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with
-- src:14376 | subsection (1) or (2) or any company that fails to comply with
-- src:14377 | subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:14378 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:14379 | term not exceeding 3 years and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:14380 | a further fine of $1,000 for every day during which the offence
-- src:14381 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 165(9) (src:14375-14381)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company that fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 165(9) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` OR `the person is a company that fails to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2) or any company that fails to comply with subsection (3) shall be guilty" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i), fork F-165-9 in NOTES.md)

-- src:14375 | (9) Any director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with
-- src:14376 | subsection (1) or (2) or any company that fails to comply with
-- src:14377 | subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:14378 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:14379 | term not exceeding 3 years and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:14380 | a further fine of $1,000 for every day during which the offence
-- src:14381 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 165(9) (src:14375-14381)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company that fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 165(9) penalty`
`s 165(9) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with subsection (1) or (2)` OR `the person is a company that fails to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST (`s 165(9) penalty` OF 15000, 3, 1000)   -- "a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of the director, chief executive officer or company named in the subsection

-- src:14375 | (9) Any director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with
-- src:14376 | subsection (1) or (2) or any company that fails to comply with
-- src:14377 | subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:14378 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:14379 | term not exceeding 3 years and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:14380 | a further fine of $1,000 for every day during which the offence
-- src:14381 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 165(9) (src:14375-14381)
GIVEN `the number of days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 165(9) the further fine for the days the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the offence continues after conviction` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN 1000 TIMES `the number of days the offence continues after conviction`
    ELSE 0
